      "calculationScope": "EXACT_MANUAL_CALCULATION",
      "manualArithmetic": "Source actual tenfold intensity gives10*log10(10)=10dB, requiring no general numerical logarithm. Echo d=c*dt/2 follows summing equal outward/return times for fixed reflector and coincident fixed emitter/receiver in a stationary uniform medium; toy300m/s and2s gives300m. Stationary-interface frequency is continuous, wavelength follows speed. Doppler is derived from successive emission positions: lambda_forward=(c-vs)/f and lambda_back=(c+vs)/f. The diagram has source advance13px per cycle against sound travel23px, hence subsonic13/23 and spacings10px/36px. These are geometric ratios, not assigned absolute speeds/frequency. Receiver radial motion and source radial motion are conceptually distinct; no numerical Doppler exercise or arbitrary decimal logarithm is assigned.",
      "manualFeasibility": "PASS_AI_EXACT",
      "physicalAssumptions": "Echo formula assumes stationary uniform propagation and fixed reflector/coincident stationary source/receiver; no unaccounted wind or moving-boundary correction. Decibel intensity ratio is positive/dimensionless with sameunits, reference1e-12W/m² inair. Intensitylevel isnot perceived loudness or pressurelevel. Doppler diagram explicitlysubsonic, classical medium andradial directions; transverse motion needs the stated usual radial approximation, not relativistic transverseDoppler.",
      "pedagogicalReview": "Separatesmediumspeed, fixed-interfacefrequency, echodoublepath andlogarithmicratio.10dB relation is exactly manual. Qualitative Doppler usesemissiongeometry andreceiver frontcount ratherthan relativevelocitywithoutmediumreference. Perception isnot equatedwithphysicalintensity.",
