      "manualArithmetic": "Independent survival law solves dN/dt=-lambda_d*N, with activity-lambda derivative positive. At ln2/lambda_d the expected population and activity halve; alternate2^(-t/T_half) is algebraically equivalent. Actual figure has32/16/8 dots explicitly labelled expected counts, not guaranteed realizations. Finite decay probability is1-exp(-lambda_d*dt), with lambda_d the infinitesimal rate; replacing it by lambda_d*dt for longintervals is excluded. Reviewer binomial variance at32 nuclei andhalf survival is8. Toy80Bq,quarter efficiency and3/s background gives23/s measured; subtracting3 and dividingbyonequarter recovers80Bq. Alpha daughter losesA4,Z2; beta-minus neutron toproton+electron+antineutrino conserves charge andleptonnumber, beta-plus reverses withpositron+neutrino; gamma changesexcitationenergy without A/Z change. Numeric nuclear examples are reviewer checks, not source assignments.",
